__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# Build output, listed per package and ALWAYS anchored.
#
# Never write these as bare `build/` or `dist/`. An unanchored `build/` also
# matches `python/src/vicary/build/` — the gazetteer builder — and silently kept
# it out of all 17 commits before the first push. A local run cannot see it: the
# files are on disk either way, imports resolve, and setuptools even puts them in
# a locally built wheel, because it reads the working tree rather than the index.
# `python/tests/test_packaging.py` is the guard; this comment is why it exists.
#
# Adding a language means adding its output here, anchored, not relaxing these.
#
# The two ROOT entries are not hypothetical. `/build/` and `/dist/` are where
# setuptools wrote before the Python package moved into `python/`, and the move
# commit swept two 0.1.1 release artifacts into the index at `dist/` — 4.8 MB of
# superseded wheel and sdist sitting at a public repository's root, which reads
# like a release channel and is not one. Anchored entries are the fix; an
# unanchored `dist/` would have matched a package named `dist`.
/build/
/dist/
/python/build/
/python/dist/
/python/.venv/
/typescript/dist/
/typescript/dist-test/
/typescript/node_modules/
/ruby/pkg/
/ruby/*.gem

# Vendored asset copies. Reproduced from `asset/` — the tracked, canonical output
# of the build mechanism — by each package's sync step, and NOT tracked: a second
# tracked copy is a second thing to bump per asset cut, which is how two front
# doors end up shipping different gazetteers.
#
# All THREE are listed, Python included. The Python copy used to be the tracked
# original that the other two vendored from, which made one of three equal front
# doors the owner of the shared input. The cost of the symmetry is that a wheel
# built without `just asset-sync` ships no gazetteer; `python/tests/test_packaging.py`
# and CI's python-build job both fail when it does.
/python/src/vicary/data/
/typescript/assets/
/ruby/assets/

.tox/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
